From: SP11 audio reverse-engineering <sp11-audio@local>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 12:40:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: audioreach: accept SH_MEM_PUSH_MODE topology endpoints

Windows MicArray EP16 terminates at MODULE_ID_SH_MEM_PUSH_MODE
(0x07001007).  The AudioReach topology loader currently accepts WR/RD shared
memory endpoints and SH_MEM_PULL_MODE as buffer/AIF widgets, but rejects the
push-mode module before a graph can be opened.

Add the authoritative module ID and treat it like the other shared-memory
endpoints at topology-load time.  This patch intentionally does not invent the
runtime circular-buffer configuration; that remains gated on a captured
Windows PARAM_ID_SH_MEM_PULL_PUSH_MODE_CFG transaction.

---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.h
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.h
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@
 #define MODULE_ID_PCM_ENC		0x07001004
 #define MODULE_ID_PCM_DEC		0x07001005
 #define MODULE_ID_SH_MEM_PULL_MODE	0x07001006
+#define MODULE_ID_SH_MEM_PUSH_MODE	0x07001007
 #define MODULE_ID_PLACEHOLDER_ENCODER	0x07001008
 #define MODULE_ID_PLACEHOLDER_DECODER	0x07001009
 #define MODULE_ID_I2S_SINK		0x0700100A
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/topology.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/topology.c
@@ -1033,6 +1033,7 @@
 	case MODULE_ID_WR_SHARED_MEM_EP:
 	case MODULE_ID_RD_SHARED_MEM_EP:
 	case MODULE_ID_SH_MEM_PULL_MODE:
+	case MODULE_ID_SH_MEM_PUSH_MODE:
 		/*
 		 * Shared-memory endpoints have no endpoint-specific topology
 		 * tokens.  The common loader above has already populated the
